7edf\u5bf9\u63a5\u3002","reasoning_content":"The user is asking for a requirements definition document in Markdown format. This is a writing task, not a coding task. They just want the complete document output directly. Should I write it as a file, or output it directly? They said \"\u8bf7\u76f4\u63a5\u8f93\u51fa\u4e00\u4efd\u89c4\u8303\u3001\u5b8c\u6574\u7684\u9700\u6c42\u6587\u6863\uff08Markdown \u683c\u5f0f\uff09\" \u2014 meaning \"please output it directly.\" So I should output text. However, the system prompt says responses should be concise, under 4 lines... but the user is explicitly requesting a complete document, which falls under \"unless the user asks for details.\" The user is explicitly asking for the complete document, so I should output it.\n\nShould I write it to a file? The user said \"\u76f4\u63a5\u8f93\u51fa\" (output directly), so I'll output it to chat rather than to a file.\n\nLet me create a standard Software Requirements Specification (SRS) in Chinese, in Markdown: \u6587\u6863\u4fe1\u606f (document info), \u80cc\u666f\u4e0e\u76ee\u6807 (background and goals), \u89d2\u8272\u4e0e\u6743\u9650 (roles and permissions), \u529f\u80fd\u9700\u6c42 (functional requirements: application entry/input, approval flow, list search, export), \u4e1a\u52a1\u89c4\u5219 (business rules), \u975e\u529f\u80fd\u9700\u6c42 (non-functional requirements), \u72b6\u6001\u6d41\u8f6c\u56fe (state transition diagram), etc.\n\nKeep it complete and well-structured.\n","metrics":{"prompt_tokens":7662,"completion_tokens":1621,"cached_tokens":7168,"extra":{"reasoning_tokens":"<redacted>"}},"llm_call_count":1}],"final_metrics":{"total_prompt_tokens":7662,"total_completion_tokens":1621,"total_cached_tokens":7168,"total_steps":2}}